Yes, because it's courtesy of the Magic House in St. Louis, which is a children's museum.

40
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.400
And he used to work there and help build exhibits.

41
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.000
And so he also built this exhibit that they gifted to the airport.

42
00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.780
And there's a little tower.

43
00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.620
And you can pretend like you're like an air traffic controller.

44
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.720
And there's a little, you know, baggage thingy.

45
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.780
And you can get on a plane.

46
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:01.380
Yeah.

47
00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.000
And it's all like a play space.

48
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.920
And when I walked by it, I was like, God, I love that.

49
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.320
And how cool is it that every time you walk past it, you can think of your dad?

50
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:10.880
I know.

51
00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.040
I took a picture of it.

52
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.760
I'll give it to you for stories.

53
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.700
Old telephones and an airport play space in stories.

54
00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.320
Lady, I'm here for it.

55
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.040
When an airport surprises you.

56
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.000
Dot, dot, dot.

57
