897
00:43:58.300 --> 00:44:03.460
And she was telling me a story about how on Sundays when the pharmacy was closed, her

898
00:44:03.460 --> 00:44:05.300
dad would sometimes have to go do paperwork.

899
00:44:05.300 --> 00:44:11.780
And so he would bring the kids to the pharmacy and he would make them a cherry Coke or a vanilla

900
00:44:11.780 --> 00:44:13.640
Coke at the soda counter.

901
00:44:13.860 --> 00:44:22.760
And my mom said that cherry-flavored Coca-Colas, which you had to mix yourself, were more popular

902
00:44:22.760 --> 00:44:24.920
than just a regular Coca-Cola.

903
00:44:25.220 --> 00:44:33.260
So popular, in fact, that my grandfather wrote a letter to the Coca-Cola company telling them,

904
00:44:33.260 --> 00:44:39.840
I'm just one person, I'm just one pharmacist with a soda fountain, but I think that you

905
00:44:39.840 --> 00:44:42.320
should have a product called cherry Coke.

906
00:44:42.460 --> 00:44:43.220
Get out.

907
00:44:43.460 --> 00:44:43.980
Yes.

908
00:44:43.980 --> 00:44:48.320
He said, because it is my most requested item at my soda counter.

909
00:44:48.880 --> 00:44:53.180
And he wrote this whole letter saying, I really think you need a product called cherry

910
00:44:53.180 --> 00:44:53.500
Coke.

911
00:44:53.640 --> 00:44:56.360
And I don't think you should call it cherry Coca-Cola.

912
00:44:56.640 --> 00:44:58.540
You should call it cherry Coke.

913
00:44:58.840 --> 00:44:59.840
This was his big idea.

914
00:45:00.020 --> 00:45:01.320
He got a letter back.

915
00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:03.740
Like, dear sir, thank you so much.

